//? Title: Key-value memory: Explicit State, Masks and Updates
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
The original key_value experiment, with reusable native tensor components and a complete editable C++ fitting program. Source seeds, budgets, derivative checks and baseline limitations are retained.
)
\toc


> Read the component and its controls

Keys encode the first fact token; values encode the second with a shared table. Two identity-initialized learned hop rotations update the query. Empty memories read exactly zero.

The source uses128 fitting,32 validation and32 test rows from the canonical local C++ memory-task generator. This is an independent local synthetic selection, not a TensorFlow dataset replay. Three epochs of eight-row batches give48 Adam updates at .01.

The actual source graph has264 learned values. The complete program records initialization, first update, every validation epoch, final parameters and source invariance probes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/key_value_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::Diagram          d(28, 1150);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle s;
  s.width     = 12;
  s.height    = 5;
  s.font_size = 28;
  d.node("in", {-21, 0}, "Observations + lengths", s)
      .node("cell", {-7, 0}, "Separate keys and values", s)
      .node("out", {7, 0}, "Live states + readout", s)
      .node("fit", {21, 0}, "Explicit Adam writes", s)
      .edge("in", "cell")
      .edge("cell", "out")
      .edge("out", "fit")
      .save_svg("build/key_value_method.svg");
}
